Curious for feedback on this. Right now, for all of our metadata formulas, including auth-level ones like getConnectionName, sync-table ones like getSchema, and parameter autocomplete, you have to call makeMetadataFormula() yourself. This seems unnecessary, this traces back to a variety of obstacles in our SDK that are centered around the user-provided definition of a thing being the same type as the thing we use at execution time. Whenever we use factory functions, these need not be the same, we can wrap and massage, and indeed we already do this some places but not others.

The downside here is that if you need to override the connectionRequirement for a metadata formula, you will have to use makeMetadataFormula() still, because the syntax would be gnarly to allow you to specify options as well.

With this change, the usage now looks like:

```
// Old
makeParameter({type: ParameterTypeString, name: 'p', autocomplete: makeMetadataFormula(async (context, search) => ...)});

// New
makeParameter({type: ParameterTypeString, name: 'p', autocomplete: async (context, search) => ...});
```

```
// Old
export const pack: PackVersionDefinition = {
  defaultAuthentication: {
    type: AuthenticationType.HeaderBearerToken,
    getConnectionName: makeMetadataFormula(async (context, search) => {
      ...
    }),
};

// New
export const pack = coda.newPack();
pack.setUserAuthentication({
    type: AuthenticationType.HeaderBearerToken,
    getConnectionName: async (context, search) => {
      ...
    },
};
```

